// Q-164 A request that computes outlives SIGTERM: the guide says a stopping server waits for up to 10 seconds, but the wait is never reached and it runs until a second signal
// mode: script
// script: steps.sh
// open-when: still running 12 s after one SIGTERM
// fixed-when: stopped after one SIGTERM
// From FEEDBACK20.md §Q-164 (found on 9e8c2fb). Q-081 is the same for a job, which is fixed; a request is not.

route GET /forever {
    let i = 0
    while true { i = i + 1 }
    "never"
}
